+## 6. Migration and Schema Safety
+
+All migration and schema work is VERIFY-FIRST and forward-only.
+
+Before proposing or executing a migration:
+
+- Verify the active repository and worktree.
+- Verify the authoritative environment.
+- Verify the database target.
+- Inspect migration history.
+- Inspect the current database revision.
+- Compare the expected schema to the actual schema using safe read-only methods.
+- Identify existing migrations relevant to the requested change.
+- Confirm that the operation is part of the approved CURRENT PHASE.
+- Define a focused forward-only repair.
+- Define validation and rollback protection.
+
+Never:
+
+- Use `alembic stamp`.
+- Use `alembic stamp head`.
+- Stamp over a migration problem.
+- Reset migration history.
+- Delete migration history.
+- Generate speculative migrations.
+- Run unsafe automatic migrations.
+- Introduce schema drift.
+- Drop and recreate the database.
+- Delete tables, columns, constraints, indexes, or data without explicit authorization.
+- Modify a production or shared schema merely to start a worktree.
+- Claim migration success without verifying the resulting revision and schema state.
+
+Preserve completed migration reconciliation work. Repairs must move forward from verified current state.
+
+---
