+## 10. Dashboard and Tenant Boundaries
+
+Preserve strict separation among:
+
+- SNS Hospice Solutions platform-owner dashboard.
+- North East Billing biller dashboard.
+- Production tenant-agency dashboards.
+- Training and test agency environments.
+
+Never merge responsibilities, navigation, permissions, data access, user management, or operational workflows between these dashboard types without explicit authorization.
+
+**SNS platform-owner boundary**
+
+SNS Hospice Solutions staff management is limited to authorized SNS Hospice Solutions personnel.
+
+Do not introduce monitoring or management of tenant-agency personnel as a platform-owner function. Tenant organizations manage their own personnel and operations.
+
+SNS Hospice Solutions focuses on: platform health, platform administration, customer experience, authorized support, tenant configuration within approved boundaries, and security and operational integrity.
+
+**Biller boundary**
+
+North East Billing functionality must remain separate from SNS platform-owner administration, tenant clinical operations, and tenant staff-management responsibilities.
+
+**Tenant boundary**
+
+Production tenants must remain isolated according to the established multi-tenant architecture. Never weaken tenant isolation for convenience, testing, reporting, or debugging.
+
+**Training and test boundary**
+
+Test future updates in approved cloned training environments before applying them to production tenants when the established release process requires that sequence.
+
+Do not treat training or demonstration data as production data. Do not introduce real-patient information into development or demonstration environments.
+
