+# SNS Staff & Access — Implementation Checkpoint
+
+Status: **FROZEN — COMPLETE, NOT YET COMMITTED**
+Date: 2026-09-14
+Branch (worktree): `suasonns-psychic-adventure` (current session branch)
+
+---
+
+## 1. Features Completed
+
+- **Human Staff lifecycle**: Add / Edit / Change Platform Role / Suspend / Activate /
+  Disable / Revoke Access / Reset Password / Remove Staff.
+- **Ownership Continuity**: Assign Additional Platform Owner, Transfer Ownership
+  Authority, Final Active Owner protection (cannot remove/downgrade the last Owner).
+- **Delegated administration**: Platform Admin (non-Owner) can perform routine staff
+  lifecycle actions within permission ceilings; Owner is not required for routine
+  administration.
+- **Service Accounts**: filtered view of the same staff list/API
+  (`account_type=SERVICE_ACCOUNT`/`AUTOMATION_ACCOUNT`) with Responsible Owner +
+  Purpose accountability fields. Create/Edit/Role Assignment/Status/Audit/Remove
+  all verified live.
+- **API Identities**: filtered view (`account_type=API_CLIENT`) with Responsible
+  Owner + Purpose + Scope accountability fields. Create/Edit/Role Assignment/
+  Status/Audit/Remove all verified live.
+- **Audit tab**: org-wide event feed (Created/Updated/Role Changed/Suspended/
+  Enabled/Disabled/Removed/Password Reset/Access Revoked) for all account types.
+- **Catalogs (finalized, do not expand further)**: Platform → Department → Job
+  Title → Platform Role → Access Level (derived) → Account Type (separate).
+
+## 2. RBAC Model
+
+- Hierarchy: `Platform → Department → Job Title → Platform Role → Access Level`.
+- Access Level is **derived** from Platform Role (not independently settable).
+- Account Type (Human Staff / Service Account / Automation Account / API Client)
+  is a **separate axis**, not part of the role hierarchy.
+- No RBAC migration, no role consolidation, no permission refactor performed —
+  all 13 existing platform roles (Owner, Platform Admin, Platform Developer,
+  Platform DevOps, Platform QA, Platform Customer Service, Platform Implementation,
+  Platform Operations, Platform Support, Platform Billing, Platform Compliance,
+  Platform Security, Platform AI Management, Platform Auditor) remain intact.
+- Backend `VALID_ROLES` allowlist fixed to include all platform roles (was
+  previously missing 8 of them — this was a real bug fix, not a model change).
+
+## 3. Ownership Continuity Model
+
+- Multiple active Platform Owners are supported simultaneously.
+- "Assign Additional Platform Owner" and "Transfer Ownership Authority" actions
+  live on the Access tab of any staff drawer.
+- Backend enforces a **final-owner protection**: the last active Owner cannot be
+  suspended, disabled, demoted, or removed.
+- Verified live: reduced from 3 owners → 1 real owner without ever hitting a
+  zero-owner state.
+
+## 4. Delegation Model
+
+- A non-Owner Platform Admin account was created, granted delegated permissions,
+  and proven to execute real staff lifecycle actions (create, edit, suspend,
+  reset password) without Owner involvement.
+- Confirms "Platform Owner is not required to execute routine staff
+  administration" per directive.
+- Delegation test account (`delegation.validation@sns.internal`) and its
+  sub-test account have since been **fully removed** from the dev database.
+
+## 5. Lifecycle Model
+
+States: `Active → Suspended → Disabled`, plus `Revoke Access` (session/permission
+revocation independent of account status) and `Remove Staff` (soft-remove,
+appears under "Removed / Former Staff" filter). Each transition emits an audit
+event and is reflected immediately in the KPform tiles (Total/Active/Suspended
+Staff counts).
+
+## 6. Service Account Model
+
+- Not a separate creation UI by design — created via the same "Add Staff" modal
+  with Account Type = Service Account, which reveals an "IDENTITY
+  ACCOUNTABILITY" section (Responsible Owner + Purpose).
+- Profile drawer renders a "PLATFORM IDENTITY — NOT AN EMPLOYEE" section instead
+  of employee-only fields.
+- Fully verified: List, Create, Edit, Role Assignment (+ Access Level
+  re-derivation + Effective Permission Summary update), Suspend/Activate,
+  Audit trail, Remove — all live-tested and cleaned up.
+
+## 7. API Identity Model
+
+- Same pattern as Service Accounts, Account Type = API Client, with an
+  additional **Scope** field ("what it is authorized to touch").
+- Fully verified: List, Create (Responsible Owner + Purpose + Scope), Edit,
+  Role Assignment, Suspend/Activate, Audit trail, Remove — all live-tested
+  and cleaned up.
+
+## 8. Audit Integration
+
+- Reuses existing platform audit infrastructure — no new audit system built.
+- Org-wide Audit tab is the authoritative source and correctly shows every
+  lifecycle event (Created/Updated/Role Changed/Suspended/Enabled/Disabled/
+  Removed/Password Reset) for Human Staff, Service Accounts, and API Identities
+  alike, with correct actor attribution and timestamps.
+- **Known minor limitation (not fixed, not blocking)**: the per-account drawer's
+  own "Audit" sub-tab only shows the account's initial creation event and does
+  not reflect later edits/role changes/status changes for that same account —
+  even though the org-wide Audit tab shows all of them correctly. Low priority;
+  deferred.
+
+## 9. Final Status
+
+**SNS Staff & Access = COMPLETE.** All 13 required workflows (Add/Edit/Change
+Role/Ownership Continuity x2/Suspend/Disable/Revoke/Reset Password/Service
+Accounts/API Identities/Audit) proven live end-to-end with UI + backend + API +
+validation + audit event + RBAC enforcement. All test/validation data created
+during verification has been removed; the dev database is back to a clean
+state (1 real Owner account only).
+
+**Audit Logs (standalone page) = WAITING FOR DESIGN REVIEW.** Paused pending
+Figma delivery of Tailwind spec / component structure / UX flows / responsive
+layouts. No code will be written for this ahead of design approval.
